{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ושא", :translit "u'sa", :gloss "and lift / and bear"} {:he "ושא את מספר שמותם", :translit "u'sa et mispar shemotam", :gloss "and lift the number of their names"} {:he "ושא עיניך ימה וצפונה", :translit "u'sa eineicha yama v'tzafonah", :gloss "and lift your eyes westward and northward"} {:he "ראה עניי ועמלי ושא לכל חטאתי", :translit "reh an'i va'amali u'sa l'chol chatat", :gloss "see my affliction and my toil and bear all my sin"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ושא את מספר שמותם" "ושא עיניך ימה וצפונה" "ושא לכל חטאתי"]} {:kind :other, :note "Three-fold gezerah shavah on the root ושא linking our verse to Genesis 13:14 and Psalm 25:18"}], :frame {:text "The Ba'al HaTurim observes that the root ושא appears three times in Scripture and links them thematically. David was punished for counting Israel (2 Samuel 24), and in Psalm 25:18 he prays to God to bear his sin. The Ba'al HaTurim then cites the rule that one who prays should direct his eyes downward, as established in Yevamot 105b based on the verse 'My eyes and My heart will be there all the days' (1 Kings 9:3), understood as a model for prayer posture.", :sources ["2 Samuel 24" "Psalm 25:18" "Yevamot 105b" "1 Kings 9:3" "Genesis 13:14"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ושא את מספר שמותם" "ושא עיניך ימה וצפונה" "ושא לכל חטאתי"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ושא את מספר שמותם", :refs ["Numbers 3:40"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ושא עיניך ימה וצפונה", :refs ["Deuteronomy 3:27"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ושא לכל חטאתי", :refs ["Psalms 25:18"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Three-fold gezerah shavah on the root ושא linking our verse to Genesis 13:14 and Psalm 25:18", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:27:07.414657085Z", :model "glm-5.2"}